---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '@/components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '@/components/Footer.astro';
import FinalCTA from '@/components/FinalCTA.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="MONTREALITY Case Study | Fractional CMO for Music & Creator Media"
  description="How Field Vision turned a 15-year creator-led music media brand into a sponsorship business, authoring the strategy and closing its first six-figure partnership with Adobe."
>
  <Header slot="header" />

  <!-- Section 1: Hero -->
  <section class="cs-hero section">
    <div class="cs-hero-inner">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Case Study</span>
        <h1>A Business and Sponsorship Strategy for MONTREALITY</h1>
        <p class="cs-hero-desc">
          I was brought in to turn a beloved, 15-year creator-led music media brand into a business that tier-one companies would pay to partner with. I authored the full business and sponsorship strategy, led the outreach and the pitch, and closed MONTREALITY's first six-figure partnership, with Adobe.
        </p>
        <div class="cs-hero-meta">
          <div class="cs-hero-meta-item">
            <span class="cs-hero-meta-label">Company</span>
            <span class="cs-hero-meta-value">MONTREALITY</span>
          </div>
          <div class="cs-hero-meta-item">
            <span class="cs-hero-meta-label">Industry</span>
            <span class="cs-hero-meta-value">Music &amp; Creator Media</span>
          </div>
          <div class="cs-hero-meta-item">
            <span class="cs-hero-meta-label">Scope</span>
            <span class="cs-hero-meta-value">8-person independent studio</span>
          </div>
          <div class="cs-hero-meta-item">
            <span class="cs-hero-meta-label">Focus</span>
            <span class="cs-hero-meta-value">Brand Strategy &amp; Partnerships</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-hero-image">
        <div style="width:100%;height:100%;min-height:340px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#213621,#2f4a2f);">
          <span style="font-family:'Anton',sans-serif;font-size:clamp(34px,5vw,72px);color:#A5DB5D;letter-spacing:0.02em;text-align:center;line-height:1;">MONTREALITY</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 2: Results Strip -->
  <section class="cs-results-strip section">
    <div class="cs-results-strip-inner">
      <div class="cs-result-stat">
        <div class="cs-stat-num">$100K+</div>
        <div class="cs-stat-label">First Partnership, with Adobe</div>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-result-stat">
        <div class="cs-stat-num">1st</div>
        <div class="cs-stat-label">Tier-One Brand Partner</div>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-result-stat">
        <div class="cs-stat-num">15 yrs</div>
        <div class="cs-stat-label">Of Audience, Finally Monetized</div>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-result-stat">
        <div class="cs-stat-num">1</div>
        <div class="cs-stat-label">Repeatable Sponsorship Playbook</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 3: The Situation -->
  <section class="cs-section section">
    <span class="eyebrow">The Challenge</span>
    <h2>Fifteen Years of Audience, No Business Model to Match</h2>
    <p>
      MONTREALITY had spent more than a decade building one of the most respected creator-led brands in music, with an audience that artists and fans genuinely trusted. What it did not have was a way to turn that trust into tier-one revenue. The team of eight ran on reputation and relationships, without a formal business or sponsorship strategy a brand like Adobe could evaluate and say yes to.
    </p>
    <div class="cs-challenge-grid">
      <ul class="cs-challenge-list">
        <li class="cs-challenge-item">
          <div class="cs-challenge-num">1</div>
          <div class="cs-challenge-text">
            <strong>No formal business model.</strong> The brand's value lived in relationships and reputation, with nothing structured that a corporate partner could evaluate or buy.
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="cs-challenge-item">
          <div class="cs-challenge-num">2</div>
          <div class="cs-challenge-text">
            <strong>An undersold audience.</strong> Fifteen years of loyal, culturally influential audience had never been packaged into a partnership story a brand could price.
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="cs-challenge-item">
          <div class="cs-challenge-num">3</div>
          <div class="cs-challenge-text">
            <strong>No outbound motion.</strong> There was no pipeline, no pitch, and no repeatable process for reaching and closing tier-one brands.
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="cs-challenge-item">
          <div class="cs-challenge-num">4</div>
          <div class="cs-challenge-text">
            <strong>A small team with big ambition.</strong> Eight people needed a strategy they could actually run, not a deck that sat on a shelf.
          </div>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <div class="cs-callout">
        <span class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--green-lt)">The Mandate</span>
        <blockquote>
          Turn a trusted creator brand into a business tier-one partners will pay for, and prove it with a signed deal.
        </blockquote>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 4: The Approach -->
  <div class="cs-approach section">
    <div class="cs-section-inner">
      <span class="eyebrow">The Approach</span>
      <h2>Package the Trust, Then Go Sell It</h2>
      <p>
        The work started with positioning: naming exactly what MONTREALITY offered a brand that no one else could. From there we built the business and sponsorship strategy, the partnership packages, and the outbound motion, then took it to market and closed.
      </p>
      <div class="cs-phases">
        <div class="cs-phase-card">
          <div class="cs-phase-num">01</div>
          <div class="cs-phase-title">Position the Brand</div>
          <div class="cs-phase-desc">
            Defined MONTREALITY's distinct value to a corporate partner: a trusted, creator-led voice in music with 15 years of audience equity. Turned that into a sharp, buyable story.
          </div>
          <div class="cs-phase-tools">
            <a href="/services/brand-strategy-positioning" class="cs-phase-tool">Brand Strategy &amp; Positioning →</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-phase-card">
          <div class="cs-phase-num">02</div>
          <div class="cs-phase-title">Build the Sponsorship Model</div>
          <div class="cs-phase-desc">
            Designed partnership tiers, deliverables, and pricing that matched the audience's real worth, so sponsorship became a repeatable product the team could sell.
          </div>
          <div class="cs-phase-tools">
            <a href="/services/go-to-market" class="cs-phase-tool">Go-to-Market Strategy →</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-phase-card">
          <div class="cs-phase-num">03</div>
          <div class="cs-phase-title">Run the Outreach</div>
          <div class="cs-phase-desc">
            Built the target list and the pitch, then led outreach to tier-one brands, opening conversations the team had never had access to before.
          </div>
          <div class="cs-phase-tools">
            <a href="/services/go-to-market" class="cs-phase-tool">Go-to-Market Strategy →</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-phase-card">
          <div class="cs-phase-num">04</div>
          <div class="cs-phase-title">Close the Deal</div>
          <div class="cs-phase-desc">
            Led the pitch process end to end and closed MONTREALITY's first six-figure partnership with Adobe, leaving the team a playbook they could run again.
          </div>
          <div class="cs-phase-tools">
            <a href="/services/fractional-cmo" class="cs-phase-tool">Fractional CMO →</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Section 5: Visual Gallery, add when imagery is available -->

  <!-- Section 6: Before & After -->
  <section class="cs-ba section">
    <div class="cs-ba-inner">
      <span class="eyebrow">Transformation</span>
      <h2>Before &amp; After MONTREALITY</h2>
      <div class="cs-ba-grid">
        <div class="cs-ba-before">
          <div class="cs-ba-label">Before</div>
          <div class="cs-ba-item">
            <div class="cs-ba-bullet"></div>
            <div class="cs-ba-text">Fifteen years of audience with no business model attached</div>
          </div>
          <div class="cs-ba-item">
            <div class="cs-ba-bullet"></div>
            <div class="cs-ba-text">Value defined by relationships, not a sellable product</div>
          </div>
          <div class="cs-ba-item">
            <div class="cs-ba-bullet"></div>
            <div class="cs-ba-text">No pipeline or pitch for tier-one brands</div>
          </div>
          <div class="cs-ba-item">
            <div class="cs-ba-bullet"></div>
            <div class="cs-ba-text">No partnership revenue at the six-figure tier</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-ba-after">
          <div class="cs-ba-label">After</div>
          <div class="cs-ba-item">
            <div class="cs-ba-bullet"></div>
            <div class="cs-ba-text">A formal business and sponsorship strategy the team owns</div>
          </div>
          <div class="cs-ba-item">
            <div class="cs-ba-bullet"></div>
            <div class="cs-ba-text">Audience packaged into clear, buyable partnership tiers</div>
          </div>
          <div class="cs-ba-item">
            <div class="cs-ba-bullet"></div>
            <div class="cs-ba-text">A live outreach motion and a proven pitch</div>
          </div>
          <div class="cs-ba-item">
            <div class="cs-ba-bullet"></div>
            <div class="cs-ba-text">First six-figure partnership signed, with Adobe</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 7: Results Deep Dive -->
  <section class="cs-results section">
    <div class="cs-results-inner">
      <span class="eyebrow">The Results</span>
      <h2>
        The Numbers Tell the Story
      </h2>
      <p>
        A trusted brand became a business, with a signed tier-one deal to prove it.
      </p>
      <div class="cs-results-grid">
        <div class="cs-result-card">
          <div class="cs-result-metric">$100K+</div>
          <div class="cs-result-label">First Partnership</div>
          <div class="cs-result-desc">
            MONTREALITY's first six-figure sponsorship, closed with Adobe, set the floor for what the brand's audience is worth.
          </div>
          <div class="cs-result-bar"><div class="cs-result-bar-fill" style="width:100%"></div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-result-card">
          <div class="cs-result-metric">1st</div>
          <div class="cs-result-label">Tier-One Brand</div>
          <div class="cs-result-desc">
            The first tier-one partner in the brand's 15-year history, opening the door to a category of buyers.
          </div>
          <div class="cs-result-bar"><div class="cs-result-bar-fill" style="width:92%"></div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-result-card">
          <div class="cs-result-metric">15 yrs</div>
          <div class="cs-result-label">Audience Monetized</div>
          <div class="cs-result-desc">
            More than a decade of audience equity, finally packaged into a product that partners will pay for.
          </div>
          <div class="cs-result-bar"><div class="cs-result-bar-fill" style="width:84%"></div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-result-card">
          <div class="cs-result-metric">1</div>
          <div class="cs-result-label">Repeatable Playbook</div>
          <div class="cs-result-desc">
            A sponsorship model and pitch the eight-person team can run again without outside help.
          </div>
          <div class="cs-result-bar"><div class="cs-result-bar-fill" style="width:78%"></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 8: Impact -->
  <section class="cs-impact section">
    <div class="cs-impact-inner">
    <span class="eyebrow">The Impact</span>
    <h2>From Beloved to Bankable</h2>
    <p>
      MONTREALITY spent fifteen years earning something most brands never get: real trust inside music culture. The gap was never the audience. It was the absence of a business model that let a company like Adobe say yes.
    </p>
    <p>
      With a positioning platform, a sponsorship strategy, and an outbound motion in place, the brand closed its first six-figure partnership and kept the playbook. The team of eight can now sell the next one themselves.
    </p>
    <div class="cs-impact-callout">
      <div class="cs-impact-icon">🎤</div>
      <div class="cs-impact-text">
        A 15-year creator brand landed its first six-figure partnership, and kept the system to land the next.
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 9: Services Used -->
  <section class="cs-services section">
    <div class="cs-services-inner">
    <span class="eyebrow">Capabilities Applied</span>
    <h2>
      What This Took
    </h2>
    <div class="cs-services-pills">
      <a href="/services/brand-strategy-positioning" class="cs-service-pill">Brand Strategy &amp; Positioning</a>
      <a href="/services/go-to-market" class="cs-service-pill">Go-to-Market Strategy</a>
      <a href="/services/fractional-cmo" class="cs-service-pill">Fractional CMO</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 10: CTA -->
  <FinalCTA />

  <Footer slot="footer" />
</BaseLayout>
